From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:46:43 -0300
Subject: Build bundled dependencies static even in a shared build

With BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON, a dependency built from a submodule (oxen-logging,
which this build forces) becomes a shared library of its own, one that isn't
installed and conflicts with the system package.
---
 external/CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/external/CMakeLists.txt b/external/CMakeLists.txt
index b816832..c844c1d 100644
--- a/external/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/external/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+# Bundled dependencies get linked into our own libraries; built shared, they would be libraries that
+# nothing installs.
+set(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS OFF)
+
 message(STATUS "Checking submodules")
 check_submodule(CLI11)
 check_submodule(nlohmann)
